    "updated_at": "2021-09-16T23:09:38Z",
    "body": "To be clear, we do need *some* way to allow users to interface with the shell's native prompt variables, because some things simply cannot be accessed by starship (the event history number, demo-ed above, is likely the most common one).\r\n\r\nThe other solutions I can think of for this case would be:\r\n\r\n- To have starship know what text is intended to be escaped and what is not (seems messy and hard to implement)\r\n- Implement a `passthrough` module that passes its text into the prompt string without any escaping (unclear if general enough for most usage, requires a new module)",
